WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.502
-Our next guest is
an Emmy-nominated actress

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:04.137
you know from films
such as "Joker"

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.405
and "The Harder They Fall."

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.707
She's starring in the third
season of "Atlanta,"

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:09.408
which airs Thursdays on FX

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:10.977
and streams on Hulu
the next day.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:13.046
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:14.214
-What the hell's wrong with you?

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:17.616
-What?

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:19.719
-Where have you been?

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.188
-[ Sighing ]
I've been shopping.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:23.789
I was thinking
about how Grace Jones has

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:27.560
all these like male suits
and I kind of wanted one.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.996
I also got this really cool
like '80s wig.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:32.766
-It's been weeks.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.603
You give me a thumbs-up emoji?

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.238
Are you serious?

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.540
-You guys are busy.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.509
You're working.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:44.977
I was just kind of doing
my own thing.

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.346
It's not really that big
of a deal.

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.915
I mean, you guys didn't plan
for me to come here.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:50.116
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.151
our friend Zazie Beetz,
everybody.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:55.154
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:55.154 --> 00:01:03.362 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:05.498 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.899
-Welcome back!

00:01:06.899 --> 00:01:08.868
-Thank you!
-You look wonderful!

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.770
It's so wonderful to have you!
-Thank you.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.238
Thanks for having me around

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.307
for the third time.
-The third time here.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.741
And it's always nice
to have you

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:16.776
because you are a New Yorker.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.677
You grew up here
in New York City.

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.579
I have a question for you
because I'm now raising

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:21.847
New York children.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:24.350
-Good luck.
-And I was a suburban child.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:28.588
And so for me, 16, the thing
every kid in the suburb

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.656
looked forward to at 16
was getting a driver's license

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:32.859
and I feel like New York kids,
that wasn't the case,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.761
necessarily.
-No! Absolutely not.

00:01:35.761 --> 00:01:38.465
I got my license
three years ago.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.400
My mom got hers a year
after I got mine.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.568
[ Laughter ]
-Okay. And she is older.

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.403
[ Laughter ]
-She's older than me.

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.238
-Okay, gotcha.

00:01:46.238 --> 00:01:48.674
-And I think back
to like high school,

00:01:48.674 --> 00:01:51.810
I think, if I remember,
out of my whole class,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.181
only one person got their
license and he drove to prom.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.482
[ Laughter ]
-Whoa.

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.284
-Everybody was like, "Yes!"
-It made it worth it.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.420
-The thing about "Atlanta"
that's fascinating --

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.254
it's been four years
since the last season,

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.723
which is both way too long

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:05.991
and also,
the minute it came back,

00:02:05.991 --> 00:02:07.827
it was familiar and comfortable
and wonderful.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:11.997
Like it is such a special show
in that it didn't --

00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:13.833
You were immediately
right back in it.

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:16.969
But even you, as a cast member
in the show, were waiting.

00:02:16.969 --> 00:02:19.539
-Yeah.
-You had an instagram post of --

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.607
This is basically
you made some reference

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:22.741
to the fact
this is how you felt,

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:24.710
waiting four years for "Atlanta"
to come back on.

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:27.413 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, it was a long four years.

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:29.415
-It was a long four years.
Now, I have a question

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.416
about one thing in this picture.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.085
Do you want to guess what it is?

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:34.353
-The, um,

00:02:34.353 --> 00:02:36.555
masks on my ears?

00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.191
-Yeah! So,
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:40.627
you have two.
Those are masks.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:41.928
-They are masks.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:44.397
-Because you misunderstood
the rules about COVID.

00:02:44.397 --> 00:02:47.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.270
-So, actually,
during Season 3,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:53.640
he cast had a --
well, we were really bonding,

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.909
so we had a tattoo
and piercing party

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:59.945
and I'm not tattooed,

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:03.683
but they all got matching
tattoos for the show.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:07.954
And I was, like, "I don't want
ink, but I'll get pierced,"

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:10.123
so they got a piercer for me

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:14.059
and I got my second
lobe piercings.

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:17.663
But it took so long
for them to heal.

00:03:17.663 --> 00:03:21.367
Like this, I think,
is nine months in

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.736
-That's way too long, right?
-and I was so frustrated.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:25.538
It's supposed to take
like six weeks.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.906
And I was so frustrated.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.441
They kept getting irritated,
so I was like,

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:31.878
"I'm sleeping with masks
on my ears."

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:33.946
You know, I don't know.
I was desperate.

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.381
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.549
That's the pandemic for you.

00:03:37.549 --> 00:03:40.953
[ Laughter ]
And so that lasted
a couple of weeks

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.756
and, yeah, I've moved on.

00:03:43.756 --> 00:03:45.958
[ Laughter ]
-Do you now have some
follow-up questions

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.127
for the piercer they found you,
that they brought in,

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:50.797
who did this excellent work?
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.531
I mean, she was British, so,

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:54.066
maybe they just do things
differently there.

00:03:54.066 --> 00:03:56.101
[ Laughter ]
-With the exchange rate,

00:03:56.101 --> 00:03:58.504
it heals longer, yeah.
-Yeah, exactly, so.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.207
You shot an episode --
you shot a season in Europe

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:03.976
and you shot an episode
in Amsterdam.

00:04:03.976 --> 00:04:06.479
I used to live in Amsterdam.
Did you enjoy the city?

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.414
-I did.
It's interesting

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.483
because New York is
New Amsterdam,

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:15.521
so some of the architecture,
I found, was sort of similar,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:19.625
I guess like the brownstone
sort of thing.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:22.662
And I actually recently met
another comedian

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.330
who also spent a year
in Amsterdam.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.599
Is that like a thing?
-Yeah, there was a comedy place

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.767
over there, so I bet it's --
-Like it's a little random.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.669
[ Laughter ]
-It's a little random, yeah.

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:32.638
Yeah, there's this comedy
theater called Boom Chicago,

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:34.841
so I bet it's somebody, yeah,
that I probably

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.241
crossed paths with.
-I was actually surprised

00:04:36.241 --> 00:04:37.209
at how diverse it was.

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.444
I wasn't really expecting that.

00:04:39.444 --> 00:04:43.982
And, you know, it's very --
I think it's beautiful.

00:04:43.982 --> 00:04:46.118
It's very sterile.
-Yes.

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:49.455
-It's very like they're very
organized and very --

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.657
and there's a reason, I think,
why people like it, but.

00:04:51.657 --> 00:04:54.226
I think I'm a little grungier.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:55.828
But it was nice.
I did enjoy it.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:58.030
-You have family in Germany.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.365
-You used to visit there
every summer.

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:00.766
-Yeah.
-I know it was the middle

00:05:00.766 --> 00:05:02.067
of the pandemic,
but did you get

00:05:02.067 --> 00:05:03.536
to visit some family?
-I did.

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.637
Right after we
finished shooting,

00:05:05.637 --> 00:05:07.607
my 30th birthday was coming up,

00:05:07.607 --> 00:05:11.410
so I went and and did it
with my grandparents.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:12.979
They're getting older,

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.548
so I don't know how many
birthdays I have with them.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:19.418
My mom was upset about that
because I wasn't home,

00:05:19.418 --> 00:05:21.421
but I'm glad I got to do it
with them

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.722
and my dad was able to come.

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:24.356
So, yeah,
I was in Germany for that.

00:05:24.356 --> 00:05:25.557
-That's nice.
We've talked in the past

00:05:25.557 --> 00:05:27.559
about your younger brother
-Fifteen now.

00:05:27.559 --> 00:05:29.595
-is a fan of your work
Fifteen now.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:32.065
And like at the time
that we first talked,

00:05:32.065 --> 00:05:35.535
a lot of what you did maybe
wasn't age-appropriate for --

00:05:35.535 --> 00:05:37.069
might've been 10 or 11
at that point.

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:38.637
-Yeah.
-And how's he doing now?

00:05:38.637 --> 00:05:40.406
Is there stuff you're doing
that he's into?

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.007
-I mean,
he's into everything now,

00:05:42.007 --> 00:05:43.976
which is so fun to share.

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:47.113
I think my mom let him watch
"Deadpool,"

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.848
[ Laughter ]
but, you know.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:50.750
-I mean, if your sister's
in "Deadpool,"

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.318
you got to watch "Deadpool."

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:53.552
[ Laughter ]
-And I mean, at that age,

00:05:53.552 --> 00:05:55.053
it's not like they're like not,
you know --

00:05:55.053 --> 00:05:57.657
What are they doing in school?
Who knows?

00:05:57.657 --> 00:06:01.260
[ Laughter ]
No, my six year old,
we walk to school

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.829
and he hears all the words.

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:04.897
-Yeah. He knows all the words.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:08.266
-I'm sure one or two
slipped out by now.
-Yeah.

00:06:08.266 --> 00:06:11.637
-But, yeah, my brother,
he loves "Invincible" a lot.

00:06:11.637 --> 00:06:13.172
That's an animated show
that I do,

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:14.773
but it's an adult animated.

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.142
It's on Amazon.
Check it out.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.843
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.345
And "Deadpool."

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.913
I mean, I think, now,
as he gets older, too,

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.349
I think a lot of this stuff
probably went over his head

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:28.387
and now I think he can engage,
maybe, a bit more,

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:29.955
I guess better
with the material.

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:34.060
But, yeah, I mean,
I'm excited to,

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:36.328
to just continue to share
that with him.

00:06:36.328 --> 00:06:39.898
And I just did a children's
movie, "The Bad Guys."

00:06:39.898 --> 00:06:41.300
-Oh, there you go.
-Yes.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.969
-I'm very excited.
My kids are very excited

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:44.170
about "The Bad Guys."
-Do they read the books?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.538
-No, but they've seen the poster

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.906
and they're just super
into the idea.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.608
They hate books.

00:06:48.608 --> 00:06:50.175
[ Laughter ]
No.
-They don't?

00:06:50.175 --> 00:06:53.546
-No, I know those are super
popular books for kids, so,

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:55.114
maybe we'll do that, first,
and then go see the movie.

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:57.917
-It's kind of like I think
it's like an introduction

00:06:57.917 --> 00:07:00.386
to the heist genre for children.

00:07:00.386 --> 00:07:02.722
It's like "Ocean's Eleven,"
but animated.

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:04.790
-See, we taught them
to steal even younger.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.958
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, good. My dad did the same.

00:07:06.958 --> 00:07:10.262
My dad forced me to steal
a Starburst from a store once.

00:07:10.262 --> 00:07:11.230
-Really?!
-Yeah.

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.498
And I felt really bad about it.

00:07:12.498 --> 00:07:15.368
He was like, "Do it!
It's good!"

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:16.935
[ Laughter ]
I think he wanted

00:07:16.935 --> 00:07:18.170
to build my character.

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:20.272
[ Laughter ]

00:07:20.272 --> 00:07:23.876
-Wow, I feel like we got
to something at the end

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:26.212
that we probably could've used
like another hour to unpack.

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:28.381
-Yeah.
-Does your dad know?

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:29.982
Is this the first time
you've admitted this story

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.917
about your dad?
-Publicly, yes.

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:32.751
[ Laughter ]
So.

00:07:32.751 --> 00:07:33.985
-Did he say afterwards, like,

00:07:33.985 --> 00:07:35.654
"Don't tell anybody!"?

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:37.990
-No, I think he was --
I don't know

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:41.227
if he needed the thrill and was
using me as a vehicle for it.

00:07:41.227 --> 00:07:43.529
[ Laughter ]
-Gotcha.
-I was eight.

00:07:43.529 --> 00:07:45.097
So, yeah.
-The interesting thing is

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:47.199
I don't think there's
a healthier option.

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:48.600
You know, like if you asked him
and he's like,

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:51.203
"No, no, no, it wasn't.
I just needed a thrill for me."

00:07:51.203 --> 00:07:53.238
[ Laughter ]
-I have therapy tomorrow,

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:54.774
so maybe I'll bring that on up.

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.408
-And the next time you're here,
let us know how you went.

00:07:56.408 --> 00:07:57.876
[ Laughter ]
Alright. Great.
Thank you so much.

00:07:57.876 --> 00:07:58.878
It's great to see you!

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:00.212
You guys, Zazie Beetz,
everybody.

00:08:00.212 --> 00:08:01.680
[ Cheering and applause ]
New episodes of "Atlanta"

00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:04.684
air Thursdays at 10:00 pm on FX
and Stream the next day on Hulu.

